      "writtenOn": "2022-01-06T17:17:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I see measurable difference for how fast memory is reclaimed when I run lmkd_unit_test to stress memory. Without this one-line change process_mrelease and exit_mmap will block each other, so memory can\u0027t be reclaimed in parallel from both threads. With this change I\u0027m reusing the same mechanisms oom-reaper uses to avoid this issue but mhocko@ rejected my proposal to do this for process_mrelease. I\u0027ll keep looking for an alternative (see discussion in https://lore.kernel.org/all/YbHIaq9a0CtqRulE@dhcp22.suse.cz/)",
      "parentUuid": "59d6ce3b_fa6280c0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9,
